      "message": "Prefer `std::span` over a raw `(uint8_t* data, uint16_t length)` pointer+length pair — e.g., splitting into `ControlTransferOut(..., std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data, ...)` and `ControlTransferIn(..., std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, ...)` (matching `util/focaltech/usb_transport.h` and `util/egis/usb_comm.h`).\n\nThat prevents buffer/length mismatches, lets zero-length control requests pass `{}` instead of `(nullptr, 0)`, and avoids forcing callers like `dfu_download()` to `const_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e` read-only firmware buffers (keeping the `libusb_control_transfer()` C API cast and `UINT16_MAX` length check isolated inside `RtsLibusbBackend`).",
