      "side": 1,
      "message": "Boot ROM runtime (`R_INITVTOR \u003d\u003d 0x00000000`) and Flash Image runtime (`R_INITVTOR \u003d\u003d 0x01800000`) both enumerate as `0BDA:5817`.\n\nIn `rtsflash.py` (`RtsUsb.get_mode()` / `enable_download()`), the host first reads `0x401E2090` (`R_INITVTOR`) via vendor request `0x41` (`RTS_VREQ_XMEM_READ`, `bmRequestType \u003d 0xC0`) and only sends `0x1A` / `0x1B` when `mode \u003d\u003d \"ROM\"`. Because `0x1A` / `0x1B` use `bmRequestType \u003d 0x80` / `0x00` (Standard Device requests), a Zephyr Flash Image implementing standard USB Chapter 9 + USB DFU Runtime without the Boot ROM\u0027s custom `0x1A` request will `STALL` (`LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE`), causing `enable_download()` to abort before `dfu_detach()` can be sent.\n\nPlease check `0x401E2090` via `0x41` like `rtsflash.py` so `0x1A` / `0x1B` are only sent in Boot ROM mode (and if a Flash Image `STALL`s `0x41` / `0x1A` with `LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE`, allow proceeding to standard `DFU_DETACH` rather than failing).",
